From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NuxFX contributors
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 03:50:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] dzn: say once that transform feedback is not implemented

The VK_EXT_transform_feedback entrypoints are stubs (patch 09): stream output is dropped. They have
to stay, because vkd3d-proton refuses to create a D3D12 device without the extension and its
transformFeedbackQueries property. An application that really writes through transform feedback
(D3D11 stream output in DXVK, D3D12 SO targets in vkd3d-proton) then gets nothing in its buffers
and nothing in the log.

The first call of vkCmdBindTransformFeedbackBuffersEXT, vkCmdBeginTransformFeedbackEXT or
vkCmdDrawIndirectByteCountEXT now prints one line:

    dzn: VK_EXT_transform_feedback is not implemented: stream output is dropped

Applications that do not use transform feedback never call these entrypoints and see no change.
---
 src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_cmd_buffer.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_cmd_buffer.c b/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_cmd_buffer.c
index 618e676..8963078 100644
--- a/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_cmd_buffer.c
+++ b/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_cmd_buffer.c
@@ -27,6 +27,8 @@
 #include "vk_debug_report.h"
 #include "vk_format.h"
 #include "vk_util.h"
+#include "util/log.h"
+#include "util/u_atomic.h"
 
 #include "dxil_spirv_nir.h"
 
@@ -6140,6 +6142,16 @@
    cmdbuf->state.dirty |= DZN_CMD_DIRTY_STENCIL_REF;
 }
 
+/* The transform feedback entrypoints below are stubs. Say so once, the first time an application
+ * uses them, so that dropped stream output shows up in the log and not only in a wrong picture. */
+static void
+dzn_warn_transform_feedback_stub(void)
+{
+   static int warned;
+   if (p_atomic_cmpxchg(&warned, 0, 1) == 0)
+      mesa_logw("dzn: VK_EXT_transform_feedback is not implemented: stream output is dropped");
+}
+
 /* VK_EXT_transform_feedback: dzn has no stream-output lowering yet. The
  * entrypoints exist so the extension can be advertised; vkd3d-proton refuses
  * to create a D3D12 device without it. Stream output is dropped, not emulated. */
@@ -6151,6 +6163,7 @@
                                        const VkDeviceSize *pOffsets,
                                        const VkDeviceSize *pSizes)
 {
+   dzn_warn_transform_feedback_stub();
 }
 
 VKAPI_ATTR void VKAPI_CALL
@@ -6160,6 +6173,7 @@
                                  const VkBuffer *pCounterBuffers,
                                  const VkDeviceSize *pCounterBufferOffsets)
 {
+   dzn_warn_transform_feedback_stub();
 }
 
 VKAPI_ATTR void VKAPI_CALL
@@ -6202,6 +6216,7 @@
                                 uint32_t counterOffset,
                                 uint32_t vertexStride)
 {
+   dzn_warn_transform_feedback_stub();
 }
 
 /* VK_KHR_maintenance6 (core 1.4) command variants. The common runtime forwards
